<article class="env-lemma" id="0AFF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AFF">Lemma <span data-tag="0AFF">29.35.21</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a smooth morphism of locally Noetherian schemes. For every point $x$ in $X$ with image $y$ in $Y$, </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \dim _ x(X) = \dim _ y(Y) + \dim _ x(X_ y),  \]
</div>
  <p> where $X_ y$ denotes the fiber over $y$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      After replacing $X$ by an open neighborhood of $x$, there is a natural number $d$ such that all fibers of $X \to Y$ have dimension $d$ at every point, see Lemma <a href="/tag/02G1" data-tag="02G1">29.35.12</a>. Then $f$ is flat (Lemma <a href="/tag/01VF" data-tag="01VF">29.35.9</a>), locally of finite type (Lemma <a href="/tag/01VE" data-tag="01VE">29.35.8</a>), and of relative dimension $d$. Hence the result follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0AFE" data-tag="0AFE">29.30.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>